  "summary": "Constraint-aware generators for 3D molecules and conjugates now appear alongside PBPK-based exposure re-scoring of generated PARP1 candidates.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is conditioning generative models on explicit constraints. PharmaDiff conditions 3D molecular diffusion on pharmacophores in a ligand-based setting, while PFM uses a perturbed conditional probability path for protein pocket-conditioned flow matching and reports a Vina score of -7.12. CupOFMoCA addresses a different constraint class, enforcing cross-component chemical constraints in discrete flows to assemble PROTAC and peptide-drug conjugates with improved validity. What is new in this set is evaluation. A PBPK-based study re-scores PARP1 generated molecules and shows that dose-driven exposure and safety limits reshuffle which candidates appear promising. Taken together, these items suggest that judging generators is shifting toward downstream pharmacokinetic and safety criteria rather than docking-style scores alone. None of the summaries report experimental validation of generated molecules, so these criteria remain computational.",
